# My Extension

A cross-browser web extension built with [WXT]({{ "https://wxt.dev" }}) and
**{{ variables.ui_framework }}**. One codebase ships to **{{ variables.build_targets }}**.

## Develop

```bash
npm install            # also runs `wxt prepare`
npm run dev            # launches a browser with HMR (target: {{ variables.target_browser }})
npm run dev:firefox    # develop against Firefox
```

`npm run dev` opens a dev browser with the extension loaded. Edit files under
`entrypoints/` and changes hot-reload.

## Project layout

```
entrypoints/        # every extension surface (manifest is generated from these)
  background.ts     # service worker (MV3) — defineBackground()
  content.ts        # content script — defineContentScript()
  popup/            # toolbar popup (index.html + main)
utils/
  messaging.ts      # typed @webext-core/messaging protocol
  storage.ts        # typed wxt/storage items
wxt.config.ts       # manifest, permissions, modules — the single source of truth
```

## Quality gates

```bash
npm run compile      # wxt prepare && tsc --noEmit
npm run lint         # eslint
npm test             # vitest
```

## Build & ship

```bash
npm run build              # .output/{{ variables.target_browser }}-mv3/
npm run zip                # store-ready zip
npm run zip:firefox        # Firefox zip (+ sources)
```

Load the unpacked build from `.output/` while developing. See `patterns/publishing.md`
for Chrome Web Store / Firefox AMO / Edge submission.
